From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 19:55:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: don't take the API lock for NO_API_LOCK controls' GPU
 reference

With dynamic power management enabled (NVreg_DynamicPowerManagement),
rmapiPrologue() and rmapiEpilogue() acquire the RM API lock in READ mode
around every external control to reference/unreference the GPUs, even when
the control itself is flagged RMCTRL_FLAGS_NO_API_LOCK. The only such
control, NV_SEMAPHORE_SURFACE_CTRL_CMD_REGISTER_WAITER, is what nvidia-drm
calls (through KAPI) for every semaphore surface fence wait, e.g. from the
compositor's main thread for every explicit-sync client buffer. It thereby
waits for every API lock writer: measured 15-25 ms per GL client exit
(KWin's main thread blocked in DRM ioctl 0x55 while glmark2 freed its device
under the API lock), twice per exit.

REGISTER_WAITER only works on semaphore surfaces, which are restricted to
sysmem, and CPU-side waiter lists and notifications, so it doesn't need the
GPU awake. Skip the GPU access reference (and with it the API lock) for
controls flagged NO_API_LOCK.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/nvidia/src/kernel/rmapi/control.c | 23 +++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/nvidia/src/kernel/rmapi/control.c b/src/nvidia/src/kernel/rmapi/control.c
index 39c9614d..faa75611 100644
--- a/src/nvidia/src/kernel/rmapi/control.c
+++ b/src/nvidia/src/kernel/rmapi/control.c
@@ -595,10 +595,24 @@ _rmapiRmControl(NvHandle hClient, NvHandle hObject, NvU32 cmd, NvP64 pUserParams
             }
         }
 
+        //
+        // With dynamic power management, rmapiPrologue() and rmapiEpilogue()
+        // take the API lock (READ) to reference/unreference the GPUs, so even
+        // a NO_API_LOCK control waits for every API lock writer (e.g. another
+        // process freeing a device, tens of ms). The only NO_API_LOCK control,
+        // the semaphore surface REGISTER_WAITER, works on sysmem semaphores and
+        // CPU-side waiter lists and doesn't need the GPU awake: skip the
+        // reference for it.
+        //
+        const NvBool bSkipGpuAccessRef = (getCtrlInfoStatus == NV_OK) &&
+                                         ((ctrlFlags & RMCTRL_FLAGS_NO_API_LOCK) != 0);
         RM_API_CONTEXT rmApiContext = {0};
-        rmStatus = rmapiPrologue(pRmApi, &rmApiContext);
-        if (rmStatus != NV_OK)
-            goto epilogue;
+        if (!bSkipGpuAccessRef)
+        {
+            rmStatus = rmapiPrologue(pRmApi, &rmApiContext);
+            if (rmStatus != NV_OK)
+                goto epilogue;
+        }
 
         //
         // If this is an internal request within the same RM instance, make
@@ -634,7 +648,8 @@ _rmapiRmControl(NvHandle hClient, NvHandle hObject, NvU32 cmd, NvP64 pUserParams
         rmStatus = serverControl(&g_resServ, &rmCtrlParams);
 
 epilogue:
-        rmapiEpilogue(pRmApi, &rmApiContext);
+        if (!bSkipGpuAccessRef)
+            rmapiEpilogue(pRmApi, &rmApiContext);
     }
 done:
 
